2026-11-12T23:38:52.450	{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Etrhca4DKAhz4DC5sDB4uQ","type":"tool_result","content":"429\t#### 8.0-8 Manager Round Routine and Control\n430\t\n431\tThe standing routine every round brief points to; briefs list only the round's tasks.\n432\t\n433\t**Round content, projects, records.** A round is launched from the web (`라운드 실행`). Without a round-specific\n434\tbrief (`.aimem/briefs/manager-round<N>-<date>.md`) the standard brief `.aimem/briefs/manager-round-standard.md` is\n435\tused and **the round's tasks are the `NEW` requests**; with nothing to do the Manager reports and ends.\n436\t- **A project spans rounds.** Each request names a project (`project` in the request file; empty = the fleet's own\n437\t  code, changed in place). Deliverables accumulate in **`projects/<project>/`** across rounds - one place, edited\n438\t  in place, no per-round copies. `projects/<project>/PROGRESS.md` is the project's memory: the Manager reads it at\n439\t  round start and prepends `## R<N>` (done, changed files, verification, **what remains**) at round close. Its\n440\t  top section `## 목표` is the project's goal checklist (`- [ ]` / `- [x]`): the Manager predicts the goals needed\n441\t  to finish the project on its first round and keeps the checks true every round - the web progress is\n442\t  done/total of that list (request average until the list exists). A new\n443\t  project gets a `README.md`. Assign paths to a slot with `aimem_db.py ownership set` before a worker writes\n444\t- **A round folder holds records only:** `rounds/R<N>/brief.md` (the brief as sent), `round.json` (launch time,\n445\t  open requests and their projects - written by the launcher; `task set --request` / `request set` during the\n446\t  round add theirs) and `REPORT.md` (the close report, also in the\n447\t  response body). No deliverables there; other rounds' folders are not touched\n448\t- **Identifiers stay as they are** (`8.0-3-1`); project and round are not prefixed to them. The web Fleet tab\n449\t  shows per-project progress: goals done/total (or request average), request counts, rounds worked (`round.json` + `PROGRESS.md`),\n450\t  and the latest `PROGRESS.md` entry\n451\t\n452\t**Start** (a new session is blank)\n453\t1. `fleet_ctl.py status` · `fleet.py status` · `aimem_db.py queue list` · `request list` · `slot list` ·\n454\t   `fleet.py runs --last 10` · `aimem_db.py handoff list --last 2`, then this header, `8.0`, `Section 9`. Trim\n455\t   output with `| head` / `| tail`\n456\t2. **Roster:** slots with role `(미배정 - 관리자가 다음 라운드에 정함)` or `events(kind=slot)` → set role and remark\n457\t   with `aimem_db.py slot set --slot S<n> --role \"…\" --note \"…\"`. Harness and model are not the Manager's to change\n458\t3. **NEW requests:** within scope and caps → split into subtasks → `PLANNED` → graph. **Caps are enforced by\n459\t   `fleet_graph.py new`:** new work stops at 3 graphs and 10 tasks per round; a graph that fixes review findings or\n460\t   re-reviews those fixes passes with `--followup \"<what it follows>\"` up to 6 graphs and 18 tasks. Never skip the\n461\t   re-review to stay under the cap. Otherwise\n462\t   `PLANNED` + \"next round\", mentioned in report item (5). A notification request from `슬롯 관리(웹)` is confirm →\n463\t   assign role → `DONE`. Mid-round arrivals are judged the same way at every checkpoint\n464\t\n465\t**Graph and verify rules** (standing; the round brief repeats them in Korean)\n466\t- **Free slots build and fix; paid slots (S1, S4) judge, design and review adversarially.** A build or fix given\n467\t  to a paid slot is listed with its reason in report item (6). Never move a failed free task to a paid slot\n468\t- **Small nodes:** one new file, about 200 lines, about 10 checks. Split larger work; split a file two slots\n469\t  would both write. Do not tell a worker to \"plan first\" - have it edit files right away\n470\t- **`verify` asks whether the worker did the work,** by exit code, never by grepping piped output\n471\t  (`… > /tmp/x.txt 2>&1 && …`). A node that writes checks is verified by \"it ran and the number of checks grew\",\n472\t  not \"the product passed\"; a product defect is reported `NEEDS-FIX: …` and fixed by a later node whose `verify`\n473\t  is \"all pass\". Run the `verify` command on the current tree once before using it\n474\t- **The engine fails an attempt that did nothing:** a report ending in a textual tool call (`aborted`) or a first\n475\t  attempt that touched none of its `write` paths (`no-op`)\n476\t- **Screen checks ask what is rendered** (`is_visible`, computed style, bounding boxes), not attributes; a screen\n477\t  behind login gets a check with auth on. Projects with a screen check overlap and overflow after input\n478\t- **Review copies of the repo exclude `.aimem/tls/`** and are removed by the reviewer when done\n479\t\n480\t**Graph checkpoints** (after each graph, so a cut session can resume from the DB)\n481\t- (a) `aimem_db.py task set --id T-xxx --status REVIEW|DONE` to match results\n482\t- (b) one `aimem_db.py event` line: \"G-xxx finished: per-node results, what remains\"\n483\t- (c) queue update (`queue drop`/`add`)\n484\t- (d) **close `REVIEW`**: reviewed task → DONE when the cross-review node is DONE; a request → DONE only after all\n485\t  its subtasks (closed requests take progress and ETA from the request status)\n486\t- (e) re-examine newly arrived `NEW` requests by start step 3\n487\t\n488\t**Close**\n489\t1. Full tests and linter; `aimem_db.py handoff add --bump --expect-rev N --body \"**REV N+1. …**\"` (≤1,200 chars);\n490\t   `render`; new rules registered in `8.0`. **`--expect-rev` is always given** - N is the REV this session last\n491\t   saw. A refusal means another session wrote meanwhile: re-read `handoff list --last 2` and the header, then\n492\t   decide; never retry with the new number blindly\n493\t2. `python3 tools/aimem_db.py archive` once (counts in the report), then `aimem_db.py migrate && render`\n494\t3. Report: `Status: DONE|PARTIAL|BLOCKED` + (1) task table (2) reproduced verification (3) waiting time (4) queue\n495\t   progress (5) next round's plan (6) operating metrics - slot utilization, Manager-only intervals, retries\n496\t   (7) one improvement proposal. These two are a standing duty. **No commit or push** (Claude Code does it)\n497\t\n498\t**Request lifecycle:** `NEW` (web/phone form) → `PLANNED` (Manager splits) → `IN-PROGRESS` (graph) →\n499\t`DONE`/`REJECTED` (Manager). Taeseok can edit title and body only while `NEW`.\n500\t\n501\t**Control table** - who changes what\n502\t\n503\t| Target | Changed by | Path | How the Manager learns |\n504\t| ------ | ---------- | ---- | ---------------------- |\n505\t| Slot harness and model | Taeseok | web Fleet tab / `aimem_db.py slot` | auto NEW request from `슬롯 관리(웹)`, readiness check, `events(kind=slot)` |\n506\t| Slot role, remark, assignment | Manager only | `aimem_db.py slot set`, graphs | (the web refuses with 400) |\n507\t| Request creation, editing while NEW | Taeseok | request form | start step 3 / checkpoint (e) |\n508\t| Request splitting and status | Manager | `aimem_db.py request set`, graphs | - |\n509\t| Archive run | Manager (close 2) / Taeseok (web) | `aimem_db.py archive` / `POST /api/archive` | `events(kind=archive)` |\n510\t| Fleet mode (prepare, run, stop) | Taeseok | web fleet bar | `fleet_graph run` output, rc 3 when spawning is forbidden |\n511\t| Chained rounds (`이어 달리기`) | Taeseok switches it on with a round cap and picks the targets: the fleet's own work, any number of projects, or everything | web fleet bar / `fleet_ctl.py chain` | while the targets have open requests or unchecked goals, the next round is launched when one ends; it stops itself when nothing is left, the report is not DONE, a round closed no request and checked no goal, or the cap is reached |\n512\t| Commit and push | Claude Code, with Taeseok's permission | git | - |\n513\t\n514\t### 8.1 Opening Slots\n515\t\n516\t2~5 concurrent, never more. Every instruction carries slot ID, token, REV and write scope (`0.1`); a retry states\n517\twhether the previous attempt left deliverables; `label` always starts with the slot ID. **Commit order:** finish\n518\tclean-up first (board, REV, linter, handoff) so one commit is consistent - never commit an intermediate state.\n519\t\n520\t---\n521\t\n522\t## 9. Awaiting Approval (Manager → Taeseok)\n523\t\n524\tItems stopped by `8.0-4` rule 3. Approved items leave this table and are recorded in the handoff log. The Manager\n525\tnever executes an item here on its own.\n526\t\n527\t| # | Item | Why | Risk | Status |\n528\t| - | ---- | --- | ---- | ------ |\n529\t| 1 | `python3 -m playwright install firefox` | The queue's \"run the monitor's browser checks in Firefox too\" cannot start: only chromium is installed. Installing is a hard limit (`0.2`), so R12 stopped and reported instead | Downloads ~90 MB into `~/.cache/ms-playwright`; no repo or config change. Declining only means the CSP `sandbox` directive and the ticket path stay checked in chromium alone | Waiting (R12) |\n530\t| 2 | Register the status line in `~/.claude/settings.json`: `\"statusLine\": {\"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"python3 /home/tsyi/work/ai-fleet/tools/claude_usage_statusline.py\"}` | The Fleet tab's \"Claude usage\" card (R18-R19) reads `.aimem/claude-usage.json`, which only that status-line command writes. The file does not exist yet, so the card shows \"register the status-line command\" and nothing else. Writing a user-global file outside this folder is a hard limit (`0.2`), so R19 stopped and reported instead | One line in Taeseok's own Claude Code settings; the script reads nothing but the session JSON Claude Code already hands it (no credentials) and writes one file inside this folder. Declining only means the card stays empty | Waiting (R19) |\n531\t\n532\tApproved and removed items: `retired-sections-2026-11.md` `[REV 128 내림] 9절`, `[REV 135 내림] 9절 1번`; older history in\n533\t`retired-sections-2026-09.md`.\n534\t\n535\t---\n536\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16781a09-6fd2-42bc-b068-ab130647c6e9","uuid":"fc070145-16f4-411d-9f03-a8d09e7c8ad2","timestamp":"2026-11-12T14:38:52.444Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/tsyi/work/ai-fleet/AIMEM.md","content":"#### 8.0-8 Manager Round Routine and Control\n\nThe standing routine every round brief points to; briefs list only the round's tasks.\n\n**Round content, projects, records.** A round is launched from the web (`라운드 실행`). Without a round-specific\nbrief (`.aimem/briefs/manager-round<N>-<date>.md`) the standard brief `.aimem/briefs/manager-round-standard.md` is\nused and **the round's tasks are the `NEW` requests**; with nothing to do the Manager reports and ends.\n- **A project spans rounds.** Each request names a project (`project` in the request file; empty = the fleet's own\n  code, changed in place). Deliverables accumulate in **`projects/<project>/`** across rounds - one place, edited\n  in place, no per-round copies. `projects/<project>/PROGRESS.md` is the project's memory: the Manager reads it at\n  round start and prepends `## R<N>` (done, changed files, verification, **what remains**) at round close. Its\n  top section `## 목표` is the project's goal checklist (`- [ ]` / `- [x]`): the Manager predicts the goals needed\n  to finish the project on its first round and keeps the checks true every round - the web progress is\n  done/total of that list (request average until the list exists). A new\n  project gets a `README.md`. Assign paths to a slot with `aimem_db.py ownership set` before a worker writes\n- **A round folder holds records only:** `rounds/R<N>/brief.md` (the brief as sent), `round.json` (launch time,\n  open requests and their projects - written by the launcher; `task set --request` / `request set` during the\n  round add theirs) and `REPORT.md` (the close report, also in the\n  response body). No deliverables there; other rounds' folders are not touched\n- **Identifiers stay as they are** (`8.0-3-1`); project and round are not prefixed to them. The web Fleet tab\n  shows per-project progress: goals done/total (or request average), request counts, rounds worked (`round.json` + `PROGRESS.md`),\n  and the latest `PROGRESS.md` entry\n\n**Start** (a new session is blank)\n1. `fleet_ctl.py status` · `fleet.py status` · `aimem_db.py queue list` · `request list` · `slot list` ·\n   `fleet.py runs --last 10` · `aimem_db.py handoff list --last 2`, then this header, `8.0`, `Section 9`. Trim\n   output with `| head` / `| tail`\n2. **Roster:** slots with role `(미배정 - 관리자가 다음 라운드에 정함)` or `events(kind=slot)` → set role and remark\n   with `aimem_db.py slot set --slot S<n> --role \"…\" --note \"…\"`. Harness and model are not the Manager's to change\n3. **NEW requests:** within scope and caps → split into subtasks → `PLANNED` → graph. **Caps are enforced by\n   `fleet_graph.py new`:** new work stops at 3 graphs and 10 tasks per round; a graph that fixes review findings or\n   re-reviews those fixes passes with `--followup \"<what it follows>\"` up to 6 graphs and 18 tasks. Never skip the\n   re-review to stay under the cap. Otherwise\n   `PLANNED` + \"next round\", mentioned in report item (5). A notification request from `슬롯 관리(웹)` is confirm →\n   assign role → `DONE`. Mid-round arrivals are judged the same way at every checkpoint\n\n**Graph and verify rules** (standing; the round brief repeats them in Korean)\n- **Free slots build and fix; paid slots (S1, S4) judge, design and review adversarially.** A build or fix given\n  to a paid slot is listed with its reason in report item (6). Never move a failed free task to a paid slot\n- **Small nodes:** one new file, about 200 lines, about 10 checks. Split larger work; split a file two slots\n  would both write. Do not tell a worker to \"plan first\" - have it edit files right away\n- **`verify` asks whether the worker did the work,** by exit code, never by grepping piped output\n  (`… > /tmp/x.txt 2>&1 && …`). A node that writes checks is verified by \"it ran and the number of checks grew\",\n  not \"the product passed\"; a product defect is reported `NEEDS-FIX: …` and fixed by a later node whose `verify`\n  is \"all pass\". Run the `verify` command on the current tree once before using it\n- **The engine fails an attempt that did nothing:** a report ending in a textual tool call (`aborted`) or a first\n  attempt that touched none of its `write` paths (`no-op`)\n- **Screen checks ask what is rendered** (`is_visible`, computed style, bounding boxes), not attributes; a screen\n  behind login gets a check with auth on. Projects with a screen check overlap and overflow after input\n- **Review copies of the repo exclude `.aimem/tls/`** and are removed by the reviewer when done\n\n**Graph checkpoints** (after each graph, so a cut session can resume from the DB)\n- (a) `aimem_db.py task set --id T-xxx --status REVIEW|DONE` to match results\n- (b) one `aimem_db.py event` line: \"G-xxx finished: per-node results, what remains\"\n- (c) queue update (`queue drop`/`add`)\n- (d) **close `REVIEW`**: reviewed task → DONE when the cross-review node is DONE; a request → DONE only after all\n  its subtasks (closed requests take progress and ETA from the request status)\n- (e) re-examine newly arrived `NEW` requests by start step 3\n\n**Close**\n1. Full tests and linter; `aimem_db.py handoff add --bump --expect-rev N --body \"**REV N+1. …**\"` (≤1,200 chars);\n   `render`; new rules registered in `8.0`. **`--expect-rev` is always given** - N is the REV this session last\n   saw. A refusal means another session wrote meanwhile: re-read `handoff list --last 2` and the header, then\n   decide; never retry with the new number blindly\n2. `python3 tools/aimem_db.py archive` once (counts in the report), then `aimem_db.py migrate && render`\n3. Report: `Status: DONE|PARTIAL|BLOCKED` + (1) task table (2) reproduced verification (3) waiting time (4) queue\n   progress (5) next round's plan (6) operating metrics - slot utilization, Manager-only intervals, retries\n   (7) one improvement proposal. These two are a standing duty. **No commit or push** (Claude Code does it)\n\n**Request lifecycle:** `NEW` (web/phone form) → `PLANNED` (Manager splits) → `IN-PROGRESS` (graph) →\n`DONE`/`REJECTED` (Manager). Taeseok can edit title and body only while `NEW`.\n\n**Control table** - who changes what\n\n| Target | Changed by | Path | How the Manager learns |\n| ------ | ---------- | ---- | ---------------------- |\n| Slot harness and model | Taeseok | web Fleet tab / `aimem_db.py slot` | auto NEW request from `슬롯 관리(웹)`, readiness check, `events(kind=slot)` |\n| Slot role, remark, assignment | Manager only | `aimem_db.py slot set`, graphs | (the web refuses with 400) |\n| Request creation, editing while NEW | Taeseok | request form | start step 3 / checkpoint (e) |\n| Request splitting and status | Manager | `aimem_db.py request set`, graphs | - |\n| Archive run | Manager (close 2) / Taeseok (web) | `aimem_db.py archive` / `POST /api/archive` | `events(kind=archive)` |\n| Fleet mode (prepare, run, stop) | Taeseok | web fleet bar | `fleet_graph run` output, rc 3 when spawning is forbidden |\n| Chained rounds (`이어 달리기`) | Taeseok switches it on with a round cap and picks the targets: the fleet's own work, any number of projects, or everything | web fleet bar / `fleet_ctl.py chain` | while the targets have open requests or unchecked goals, the next round is launched when one ends; it stops itself when nothing is left, the report is not DONE, a round closed no request and checked no goal, or the cap is reached |\n| Commit and push | Claude Code, with Taeseok's permission | git | - |\n\n### 8.1 Opening Slots\n\n2~5 concurrent, never more. Every instruction carries slot ID, token, REV and write scope (`0.1`); a retry states\nwhether the previous attempt left deliverables; `label` always starts with the slot ID. **Commit order:** finish\nclean-up first (board, REV, linter, handoff) so one commit is consistent - never commit an intermediate state.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Awaiting Approval (Manager → Taeseok)\n\nItems stopped by `8.0-4` rule 3. Approved items leave this table and are recorded in the handoff log. The Manager\nnever executes an item here on its own.\n\n| # | Item | Why | Risk | Status |\n| - | ---- | --- | ---- | ------ |\n| 1 | `python3 -m playwright install firefox` | The queue's \"run the monitor's browser checks in Firefox too\" cannot start: only chromium is installed. Installing is a hard limit (`0.2`), so R12 stopped and reported instead | Downloads ~90 MB into `~/.cache/ms-playwright`; no repo or config change. Declining only means the CSP `sandbox` directive and the ticket path stay checked in chromium alone | Waiting (R12) |\n| 2 | Register the status line in `~/.claude/settings.json`: `\"statusLine\": {\"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"python3 /home/tsyi/work/ai-fleet/tools/claude_usage_statusline.py\"}` | The Fleet tab's \"Claude usage\" card (R18-R19) reads `.aimem/claude-usage.json`, which only that status-line command writes. The file does not exist yet, so the card shows \"register the status-line command\" and nothing else. Writing a user-global file outside this folder is a hard limit (`0.2`), so R19 stopped and reported instead | One line in Taeseok's own Claude Code settings; the script reads nothing but the session JSON Claude Code already hands it (no credentials) and writes one file inside this folder. Declining only means the card stays empty | Waiting (R19) |\n\nApproved and removed items: `retired-sections-2026-11.md` `[REV 128 내림] 9절`, `[REV 135 내림] 9절 1번`; older history in\n`retired-sections-2026-09.md`.\n\n---\n","numLines":108,"startLine":429,"totalLines":536}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Etrhca4DKAhz4DC5sDB4uQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config",